rch in. Defaults to the current directory if not provided.\",\"optional\":true}],\"async\":null},{\"name\":\"read_buffer\",\"description\":\"Return the contents of an Emacs buffer\",\"args\":[{\"name\":\"buffer\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The name of the buffer whose contents are to be retrieved\"}],\"async\":null},{\"name\":\"EditBuffer\",\"description\":\"Edits Emacs buffers\",\"args\":[{\"name\":\"buffer_name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Name of the buffer to modify\"},{\"name\":\"old_string\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Text to replace (must match exactly)\"},{\"name\":\"new_string\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Text to replace old_string with\"}],\"async\":null},{\"name\":\"ReplaceBuffer\",\"description\":\"Completely overwrites buffer contents\",\"args\":[{\"name\":\"buffer_name\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Name of the buffer to overwrite\"},{\"name\":\"content\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Content to write to the buffer\"}],\"async\":null},{\"name\":\"eshell-command\",\"description\":\"Execute an Emacs Eshell command and return its output. Use for commands such as pwd, ls, grep, find, git status, pipelines, and redirection; it supports Eshell built-ins, aliases, and external commands.\",\"args\":[{\"name\":\"command\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The Eshell command to execute.\"}],\"async\":null},{\"name\":\"workspace_read\",\"description\":\"Read one buffer-region Artifact from the current Workspace. Cross-Run reads require the revision reported by workspace_info and are delivered only after the producer Run has a durable Closure proof.\",\"args\":[{\"name\":\"artifact_id\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Artifact ID; omit for the active Artifact.\",\"optional\":true},{\"name\":\"expected_revision\",\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Revision reported by workspace_info; required when consuming an Artifact produced by another Run.\",\"optional\":true}],\"async\":null},{\"name\":\